# Session 9 & 10 – Blog Application Backend

##  Overview
This project is a **Blog Application Backend** developed using **Node.js**, **Express.js**, and **MongoDB**. It provides API endpoints for managing blog content, handling middleware, and structuring backend logic in a scalable way.

The application follows modular backend architecture, making it suitable for real-world full-stack integration.

---

##  Features
- Create Blog Posts
- Read All Posts
- Read Single Post
- Update Existing Post
- Delete Post
- Middleware-based request handling
- Modular API routing
- Database model structure
- Server health monitoring

---

##  Project Structure

```bash
session9&10_blogapp/
│── APIs/
│── middlewares/
│── models/
│── ping/
│── package-lock.json
│── package.json
│── server.js
```

---

##  Folder Explanation

### `APIs/`
Contains:
- Blog routes
- CRUD request handlers
- API business logic

Example endpoints:
- `GET /blogs`
- `POST /blogs`
- `PUT /blogs/:id`
- `DELETE /blogs/:id`

---

### `middlewares/`
Reusable middleware for:

- Authentication
- Validation
- Logging
- Error handling
- Route protection

---

### `models/`
Contains MongoDB models such as:

### Blog Schema Example
```js
{
  title: String,
  content: String,
  author: String,
  category: String,
  createdAt: Date
}
```

Used for:
- Data validation
- Collection mapping
- CRUD operations

---

### `ping/`
Used for:
- Health check endpoint
- Server monitoring
- API uptime verification

Example:

```http
GET /ping
```

Response:

```json
{
  "message": "Server is running"
}
```

---

## 🛠 Technologies Used
- JavaScript (ES6)
- Node.js
- Express.js
- MongoDB
- Mongoose
- Middleware
- npm
- VS Code
- Git & GitHub

---

## ⚙ Installation

Clone repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/NITESHSA1/ATP_24EG106A21.git
```

Move into folder:

```bash
cd session9&10_blogapp
```

Install dependencies:

```bash
npm install
```

Run server:

```bash
node server.js
```

or

```bash
npm start
```

---

##  API Examples

### Create Blog
```http
POST /blogs
```

### Get All Blogs
```http
GET /blogs
```

### Update Blog
```http
PUT /blogs/:id
```

### Delete Blog
```http
DELETE /blogs/:id
```

